   193	## 5. Elimination: the resultants, the square system, and the top-weight trap
   194	
   195	### 5.1 The resultants
   196	
   197	For a quadratic `f=a1 b3^2+b1 b3+c1` and `g=a2 b3^2+b2 b3+c2`,
   198	`Res_b3(f,g)=(a1c2-a2c1)^2-(a1b2-a2b1)(b1c2-b2c1)` (the `2x2` Sylvester
   199	identity; checked on `x^2-1, x^2-4 -> 9` and a common-root pair `-> 0`).  With
   200	`f=T_(t,2t-1)`, `lc_b3 f = alpha_t` a unit, so `Res=0` at a point iff `f,g`
   201	share a `b3`-root there, whatever `g`'s leading coefficient does.  The
   202	resultant is isobaric: with `wt b3=t+1`, `wt(a1)=0`, `wt(c1)=2t+2`,
   203	
   204	```text
   205	wt Res_b3(T_(t,2t-1), T_(t,k)) = deg_b3(T_k)*(2t+2-2(t+1)) + 2(4t+1-k) = 8t+2-2k,
   206	```
   207	
   208	independent of `deg_b3 T_k` (2 on the top tail, 3 on `k<=t-2`).  Stage A
   209	computed all `2t-2` resultants at `t=3..7` (top tail by the formula, lower
   210	rows by Singular's `resultant`) and printed `homog=1`, `wdeg=8t+2-2k` for
   211	every one.  Sizes grow fast (`t=6`: 674..1465 terms for the top tail,
   212	1745..3262 for the lower rows; `t=7`: 1904..5402 and 7756..14778).
   213	
   214	### 5.2 Lemma SQUARE and the two charts of the resultant system
   215	
   216	Put `R_r=Res_b3(T_(t,2t-1),T_(t,2t-1-r))`, `r=1..t-1`: `t-1` forms of weights
   217	`4t+4+2r` in the `t-1` variables `b4,q_(2,0),..,q_(t-1,0)` (weights
   218	`1,2,..,t-1`).  If `(b4,q,b3) in V(T_(t,t..2t-1))` then every `R_r(b4,q)=0`;
   219	if `V(R_1..R_(t-1))={0}` then `V(top tail)` lies over `b4=q=0`, where
   220	`T_(t,2t-1)=alpha_t b3^2` kills it: `V(top tail)={0}`, hence `(V0)`, `(8.1)`,
   221	`(T)`.  The resultant system is thus a sufficient, square, `b3`-free
   222	reformulation, with its own chain: head `b4 in sqrt(R)`, i.e.
   223	
   224	```text
   225	(RH_t)  < R_1|_(b4=1), .., R_(t-1)|_(b4=1) > = (1) in A_t[q_(2,0),..,q_(t-1,0)],
   226	```
   227	
   228	and tail `V(R)|_(b4=0)={0}`.  `(RH_t)` implies `(C0)` (a point of
   229	`V(I_(t,+))` with `b4!=0` projects to a point of `V(R)` with `b4!=0`); the
   230	converse is not claimed (`V(R)` may contain points where the shared `b3`-roots
   231	differ from row to row).  The tail collapses on the proved sub-charts: on
   232	`S={b4=q_(2,0)=..=q_(t-2,0)=0}`, `t>=6`, `T_(t,2t-1)|_S=alpha_t b3^2` and
   233	`T_(t,t+4)|_S=A2 x^3` (Q-PLANE), so `R_(t-5)|_S = alpha_t^2 A2^2 x^6`, a unit
   234	times a pure power -- the chain step `(C_(t-1))` for `R`; the steps
   235	`(C_(t-r))`, `r<=5`, `t>=3r+3`, follow in the same way from UNIQUE-POWER (on
   236	`S_r'` band `2t-1` is `alpha_t b3^2` and band `t+3r+1` is `A2^(r) q_(t-r,0)^3`,
   237	so their resultant is `alpha_t^2 (A2^(r))^2 q_(t-r,0)^6`); the deeper steps
   238	are exactly as open for `R` as for `I_(t,+)`.  Fixed `t`:
   239	
   240	| test | `t=3` | `t=4` | `t=5` | `t=6` |
   241	|---|---|---|---|---|
   242	| `(RH_t)`, top-tail resultants alone, `b4=1` | **UNIT, char 0** (`D1`, instant) | INCONCLUSIVE_TIMEOUT char 0 (150 s minpoly, 240 s y-adjoined); **UNIT mod 32029** | **UNIT mod 32009** (1 s) | timeout 400 s mod 32003 |
   243	| all `2t-2` resultants, `b4=1` | UNIT, char 0 (`D2`) | -- | -- | -- |
   244	| top-weight parts `R_r|_(b4=0)`: dim in `q`-space | 0, lead `q_(2,0)^10` (char 0) | 0, 7 gens (char 0) | 0, 53 gens (char 0, 5 s) | 0, 1036 gens (mod 32003) |
   245	| top-tail rows at `b4=0`: cone dim | 0 (char 0) | 0 (char 0) | 0 (char 0) | -- |
   246	| top-tail cone `V(T_(t,t..2t-1))`, `b4` free | dim 0, `b4^21,q_(2,0)^11,b3^6` in it (char 0) | dim 0 (char 0, 54 s; power loop timed out) | dim 0 mod 32009 | dim 0 mod 32003 (39 s) |
   247	
   248	So at `t=3` the resultant route closes exactly: `V(R_1,R_2)={0}` in
   249	`A_3[b4,q_(2,0)]`, `V(top tail)={0}`, `(V0)` -- by two univariate
   250	resultants and one gcd.  At `t>=4` the char-0 head `(RH_t)` did not finish: the
   251	resultants square the coefficient sizes, and the direct chart test `D3`
   252	(top-tail rows on `b4=1`, `UNIT` in 74 s at `t=4`) is **cheaper** than its own
   253	resultant elimination (`>240` s).  The elimination is therefore a structural
   254	reformulation, not a computational shortcut; the modular `(RH_t)` results at
   255	`t=4,5` are the cheapest falsification test of the uniform target and are
   256	typed MEASURED-MODULAR (a modular unit ideal does not lift).
   257	
   258	The top-tail cone test (`F4`) is homogeneous, sits inside `I_(t,+)`, and is
   259	therefore promotable by the banked properness lemma exactly like the full
   260	cone; measured mod `p` it is not cheaper than the full cone (`t=6`: 39 s vs
   261	the gate's 12 s), so it does not open `t=8,9,11`.
   262	
   263	### 5.3 The top-weight part certifies finiteness, not emptiness
   264	
   265	Let `J=I_(t,+)|_(b4=1)`, `K=J cap A_t[q]`, or the resultant ideal, filtered by
   266	the `(q,b3)`-weight.  For a weighted form `f`, `f|_(b4=1)` has top-weight part
   267	`f|_(b4=0)`.  Hence the ideal generated by the initial forms of the generators
   268	of `J` is `I_(t,+)|_(b4=0)` -- the `b4=0` cone ideal, whose dim-0 statement is
   269	RESIDUAL-ZERO -- and for the resultants it is `<R_r|_(b4=0)>`.  Two facts:
   270	
   271	* `in_top(f|_(b4=1)) = f|_(b4=0)` whenever the latter is nonzero, so the
   272	  ideal of initial forms of the generators contains `I_(t,+)|_(b4=0)`, and
   273	  RESIDUAL-ZERO forces `dim in_top(J)=0`.  Moreover
   274	  `in_top(J) = (I_(t,+):b4^infty)|_(b4=0)` and `dim_K A[q,b3]/J = dim_K A[q,b3]/in_top(J)`
   275	  (Groebner degeneration along a positive weight).  So `dim in_top(J)=0`
   276	  (cone `={0}`) is equivalent to `V(J)` FINITE, i.e. to `V(I_(t,+))` being
   277	  `{0}` union finitely many weighted lines with `b4!=0`.  Emptiness of `V(J)`
   278	  is `in_top(J) ni 1`, i.e. `J=(1)` itself -- nothing is gained.
   279	* The inference "top-weight part has dim 0 (or RESIDUAL-ZERO holds) hence the
   280	  `b4=1` chart is unit" is FALSE.  Exact witness (`negctrl_topweight.sing`,
   281	  weights `wp(1,2,4)` as at `t=3`): `I=<q2-b4^2, b3>`.  Its `b4=0` slice is
   282	  `{0}` (`lead=b4,q2,b3`), the initial forms of `I|_(b4=1)=<q2-1,b3>` generate
   283	  `<q2,b3>` of dim 0, yet `I|_(b4=1)` is not unit (`unit=0, dim=0`: the point
   284	  `q2=1,b3=0`), `b4^N notin I` for `N<=12`, and the cone is the curve
   285	  `q2=b4^2, b3=0` (dim 1).  This is the `b4`-axis report's counterexample (4.3)
   286	  run as a Singular control.
   287	
   288	Consequently the requested "compute the top-weight part and test dim=0" is
   289	exactly the tail (RESIDUAL-ZERO / the `q`-chain), already proved on
   290	sub-charts and exact at `t<=7`; it cannot deliver `(C0)`, because `b4!=0` is
   291	open and every weight degeneration lands in `b4=0`.  `(C0)` is a statement
   292	about the closure of `V(I) cap {b4!=0}`, i.e. about `I:b4^infty`, which no
   293	initial-ideal computed from generators sees.
   294	
