   334	## 8. FALLACY-v2 checklist
   335	
   336	* Floor/attainment and sub-chart-to-full-radical: Sec. 5.3 refuses the
   337	  top-weight inference with an exact counterexample; no axis or `b4=0`
   338	  statement is promoted to `b4 in sqrt I`.
   339	* `sat()`: not used; `b4`-membership is by explicit `b4^N` reduction against a
   340	  reduced standard basis of the homogeneous ideal.
   341	* Variable/ring map: every job declares ring, generator order
   342	  `(b4,q_(2,0),..,q_(t-1,0),b3)`, weights `wp(1,..,t-1,t+1)`, and the
   343	  coefficient encoding; `imap` by name is used only between rings sharing the
   344	  names, after the driver's own eliminated-variable checks.
   345	* Denominators/split: `t=2` branched; `A_t` never inverted as a product; the
   346	  only divisions are the banked unit pivots and Singular's field arithmetic
   347	  over `Q(y)/(H_t)`; `t=3..7` are non-split.
   348	* Modular runs are labelled MEASURED-MODULAR; the promotable ones (`F4`,
   349	  homogeneous, inside `I_(t,+)`) are stated as promotable but are not used to
   350	  claim anything beyond the banked `t<=7`.
   351	* No interpolation from finite `t`: the `r=1,2` closed forms are typed OPEN
   352	  although (3.2) proves they exist; the values are exact per `t`.
