   253	### 4.4 Theorem DOMINANT-LEADER and the deep-strata chain
   254	
   255	**Theorem DOMINANT-LEADER.**  Let `<` be any monomial order on
   256	`K[x_1..x_n]`, `wt x_i = w_i > 0`.  Write `x_i >> x_j` if `x_i^{w_j} > x_j^{w_i}`
   257	(both of weight `w_i w_j`).  This is a total order on the variables (if
   258	`x_i^{w_j} > x_j^{w_i}` and `x_j^{w_k} > x_k^{w_j}`, raising to the powers
   259	`w_k`, `w_i` and multiplying gives `x_i^{w_j w_k} > x_k^{w_i w_j}`, hence
   260	`x_i^{w_k} > x_k^{w_i}`), so it has a maximum `x_*`.  For any monomial `x^m` of
   261	weight `w` with some `m_i > 0`, `i != *`: `(x^m)^{w_*} = prod x_i^{m_i w_*}
   262	< prod x_*^{m_i w_i} = x_*^{w}`, hence `x^m < x_*^{w/w_*}` whenever `w_* | w`.
   263	Therefore a form with full support and `w_* | wt` has `LM = x_*^{wt/w_*}`.  QED
   264	
   265	Consequences.  (a) In the prompt order `wp(1,2,..,t-1)` with `b4` first, and in
   266	every order with `b4` dominant, every `B_r, C_r` has leader `b4^{wt}` (this is
   267	the measured `lead=` column); no two are coprime, and the leading-monomial
   268	ideal of any subset is a single `b4`-power, of dimension `t-2`.  (b) In any
   269	order a set with pairwise coprime leaders contains at most one form whose
   270	weight is divisible by `w_*`.  So the "closed form in `t` for the leading terms
   271	of `B_r, C_r` that makes a subset an sop" (card item (2)) does not exist in the
   272	prompt order, and a Groebner-type proof of (i) has to pass through
   273	S-polynomial leaders (the pure powers `q_j^{e_j(t)}` of the table in 4.1 all
   274	arise that way, none from a generator).  The exponents `e_j(t)` are recorded
   275	as MEASURED: `b4`: `9,13,17,23,28`; `q2`: `5,7,9,12,14`; `q_{t-1}`: `5,5,5,5,5`
   276	(`t=3..7`); no formula is claimed.
   277	
   278	**Deep strata.**  On `S_rho = {b4 = q_2 = .. = q_{t-1-rho} = 0}` a monomial of
   279	`B_r` (weight `t+1+r`) has two factors of weight `>= t-rho`, three only if
   280	`3(t-rho) <= 2t`, i.e. `t <= 3 rho`.  For `t > 3 rho` the square `q_{t-j}^2`
   281	(weight `2t-2j = t+1+r` at `r = t-1-2j`, `j=1..rho`) is the only monomial of its
   282	weight in `q_{t-j},..,q_{t-1}` that does not involve a heavier stratum variable,
   283	so `B_{t-1-2j}|_{S_rho} = beta_j q_{t-j}^2 + (terms divisible by q_{t-j+1},..,q_{t-1})`
   284	and, if the `rho` scalars `beta_j` are units, `V(B) cap S_rho = {0}` by the
   285	triangular chain `q_{t-1}^2, q_{t-2}^2, .., q_{t-rho}^2`.  This is the
   286	`B`-version of the banked UNIQUE-POWER chain, with the same cap `rho < t/3`;
   287	it adds nothing beyond the banked strata results and is recorded only to show
   288	that clause (i) has the same "dense middle" as the original chain: for
   289	`rho >= t/3` the restricted forms have three-factor monomials and are no longer
   290	triangular.
