   292	## 5. Clause (ii): the rank-one curve
   293	
   294	### 5.1 Theorem FITT (exact reformulation, all t>=3)
   295	
   296	`M_t = S_t/(T_{t,2t-1})` is `P_t`-free on `{1,b3}` (TAIL-SPLIT).  Multiplication
   297	by `G_r = C_r + B_r b3` has matrix `[[C_r, -c_0 B_r/a_0],[B_r, C_r - b_0 B_r/a_0]]`
   298	(columns = images of `1`, `b3`; `b3^2 = -(b_0 b3 + c_0)/a_0`).  Hence
   299	`S_t/J_t^tail = coker( P^{2(t-1)} --[G_1|..|G_{t-1}]--> P^2 )`, whose support is
   300	`V(Fitt_0) = V(I_2[G_1|..|G_{t-1}])`.  The `2x2` minors are: within a block
   301	`det G_r = W_r/a_0`; across blocks `-(B_r C_s - B_s C_r)`, `(c_0/a_0)(B_r C_s - B_s C_r)`,
   302	`X_rs/a_0`, `-X_sr/a_0`, with `X_rs - X_sr = b_0 (B_r C_s - B_s C_r)`.  So
   303	
   304	```text
   305	F_t = I_2(N) + (W_1..W_{t-1}) + (X_rs)_{r<s},  and  V(J_t^tail) = {0} <=> V(F_t) = {0},
   306	```
   307	
   308	because `Spec S_t/J_t^tail -> Spec P_t` is finite (`b3` integral over `P_t` mod
   309	the top row) with image `V(F_t)`.  At a point `p` with `rank N(p) = 1` and kernel
   310	`(1:beta)` one has `C_r = -beta B_r`, hence
   311	`W_r = B_r^2 (a_0 beta^2 + b_0 beta + c_0) = B_r^2 T_{t,2t-1}(p,beta)` and
   312	`X_rs = B_r B_s T_{t,2t-1}(p,beta)`; with kernel `(0:1)` (all `B_r = 0`, some
   313	`C_r != 0`) `W_r = a_0 C_r^2 != 0`.  Therefore `V(F_t) = V(I_2(N) + (W))` and
   314	clause (ii) is precisely: **the top row does not vanish at the unique lift
   315	`(p, beta(p))` of any rank-1 point `p != 0`**, equivalently `T_{t,2t-1}` is a
   316	nonzerodivisor on `S_t/(G_1..G_{t-1})`.  (Verified numerically: `dim(I_2+(W)) =
   317	dim(F_t) = 0` at every tested index; `vdim(P/F_t) = 14, 105, 670, 4126, 25395`
   318	and `vdim(P/(I_2+(W))) = 14, 114, 775, 4910, 30288` for `t=2..6`.)
   319	
   320	### 5.2 Theorem EN-CURVE
   321	
   322	Suppose `V(J_t^tail) = {0}`.  Every component of `V(G_1..G_{t-1})` has
   323	dimension `>= 1` and is cut to `{0}` by the single form `T_{t,2t-1}`, so
   324	`dim V(G) = 1`: `G_1..G_{t-1}` is a regular sequence in `S_t`.  If some `p != 0`
   325	had `rank N(p) = 0`, the cone over `{p} x A^1` (dimension 2) would lie in
   326	`V(G)`; so clause (i) follows, and `V(I_2(N)) = Gamma cup {0}` with
   327	`Gamma = {rank N = 1}` of dimension `1`.  For a `(t-1) x 2` matrix the height of
   328	`I_2` is at most `t-2`; here it equals `t-2`, so `I_2(N)` is perfect and the
   329	Eagon-Northcott complex of `phi: (+)_{r} P(-(2t+2+r)) -> P (+) P(-(t+1))`
   330	(rows `(C_r, B_r)`; the column shift `t+1` is forced by `wt C_r - wt B_r = t+1`)
   331	is a minimal graded free resolution: `P_t/I_2(N)` is Cohen-Macaulay of
   332	dimension 1, `Gamma cup {0}` has no embedded component, and `Gamma` is a finite
   333	union of weighted lines through `0`.  The `k`-th EN term `wedge^{k+2}F (x)
   334	S_k(G)^* (x) wedge^2 G^*` has generators in degrees
   335	`sum_{r in R}(2t+2+r) - (j+1)(t+1)`, `|R| = k+2`, `0 <= j <= k`, so the numerator
   336	of `Hilb(P_t/I_2(N); s) = HN_t(s)/prod_{i=1}^{t-1}(1-s^i)` is
   337	
   338	```text
   339	HN_t(s) = 1 + sum_{k=0}^{t-3} (-1)^{k+1} sum_{|R|=k+2} s^{sum_R (2t+2+r) - (t+1)} [k+1]_{s^{-(t+1)}} .
   340	```
   341	
   342	**Closed form.**  Put `x_r = s^{2t+2+r}`, `y = s^{t+1}`; then
   343	`sum_{j=0}^{k} y^{-j} = (1 - y^{-(k+1)})/(1 - y^{-1})` and, with `e_m` the
   344	elementary symmetric functions and `sum_m (-1)^m e_m(x) = prod(1-x_r)`,
   345	`sum_m (-1)^m e_m(x) y^{-(m-1)} = y prod(1 - x_r/y)`,
   346	
   347	```text
   348	HN_t(s) = [ prod_{r=1}^{t-1}(1 - s^{2t+2+r}) - s^{t+1} prod_{r=1}^{t-1}(1 - s^{t+1+r}) ] / (1 - s^{t+1}) .   (EN)
   349	```
   350	
   351	`en_degree.py` checks `(EN)` against the term-by-term EN sum for `t=3..15`
   352	(zero difference) and `hilb_compare.py` checks it against Singular's
   353	`hilb(std(I_2),1,wv)` numerators at `t=3` (exact), `t=4`, `t=5` (mod `p`):
   354	identical.  Consequently
   355	
   356	```text
   357	Hilb(P_t/I_2(N)) = Hilb(S_t/(G_1..G_{t-1})) - s^{t+1} Hilb(P_t/(B_1..B_{t-1}))_CI / (1 - s^{t+1}),
   358	```
   359	
   360	where the first term is the CI series `prod(1-s^{2t+2+r})/((1-s^{t+1})prod(1-s^i))`
   361	of the `G_r` in `S_t` and the second is the CI series of forms of weights
   362	`t+2..2t` in `P_t`, tensored with `K[b3]` and shifted by `t+1`.  Multiplying by
   363	`(1-s)` and letting `s -> 1`:
   364	
   365	```text
   366	d_Gamma(t) := lim_{s->1} (1-s) Hilb(P_t/I_2(N))
   367	            = C(3t+1,t-1)/(t+1) - C(2t,t-1)/(t+1) = [C(3t+1,t-1) - C(2t,t-1)]/(t+1).
   368	```
   369	
   370	`d_Gamma` is the weighted degree of `Gamma`: a weighted line through a point
   371	with nonzero coordinates of weights `w_i` has coordinate ring `K[lambda^g]`,
   372	`g = gcd(w_i)`, hence contributes `mult/g` (orbifold points count fractionally).
   373	Values: `15/2, 46, 805/3, 1548, 35805/4, 52140, 3064347/10, 1817465`
   374	(`t=3..10`).  At `t=3` the single minor (weight 15 in `b4, q2`) factors mod
   375	`32003` as `b4 * (quartic) * (weight-10 form)` on one root and
   376	`b4 * (quadratic)^2-type * (weight-10 form)` on the other, i.e. `1/2 + 2 + 5 = 15/2`
   377	weighted points; at `t=4` the three minors give `5` prime components on one
   378	root (`mult 3,9,21,33,72`, sum `138 = mult(I_2)`) and `3` on the other
   379	(`18,39,81`), the geometric point count being `46` in both cases.
   380	
   381	### 5.3 LENGTH-SPLIT and the axis multiplicity
   382	
   383	`L_t = (2t+2) * deg_w V(G) = (2t+2) C(3t+1,t-1)/(t+1) = 2 C(3t+1,t-1)` is the CI
   384	length of the tail (top row of weight `2t+2` cutting the CI curve `V(G)`).
   385	By `(EN)`, `deg_w V(G) = d_Gamma(t) + C(2t,t-1)/(t+1)`, so
   386	
   387	```text
