   619	
   620	## 6. FALLACY-v2 Audit
   621	
   622	- Flag/place/series: the CI series `P_t`, the EN curve `Gamma`, the affine cone
   623	  `V(I_{t,+})`, and z-type chart points are kept separate.
   624	- Floor/attainment: `L_t` is used only as the length after dimension zero or a
   625	  regular-sequence hypothesis is known.  It is not used to prove dimension zero
   626	  or top-row nonvanishing.
   627	- Carrier/attainment: the EN degree counts weighted points where Target A must
   628	  be checked; it is not a witness that the top row avoids them.
   629	- `sat()` wrapping: no saturation is used.
   630	- Raw remainder degree: the only normal-form style statement used here is the
   631	  generic eliminant identity in indeterminates, reproduced by the frozen driver.
   632	- Variable/ring map: the `t=8` computations explicitly use
   633	  `GF(32003)[b3,b4,q(2),...,q(7)]` with weights `wp(9,1,2,...,7)` and the sealed
   634	  row file at root `11288`.
   635	- Prime label/derivative: `p` is always a finite-field characteristic; prime
   636	  marks from Laurent formulas are not used as derivatives here.
   637	- Modular promotion: only homogeneous cone `dim=0` statements are promoted
   638	  through the charged properness gate.  Rabinowitsch radical membership modulo
   639	  `p` is not promoted.
   640	- No interpolation: no all-t certificate is inferred from the fixed range
   641	  `t<=7`.
   642	
   643	## 7. Final Status
   644	
   645	Target A is reduced uniformly to a clean EN/incidence nonvanishing problem:
   646	
   647	```text
   648	Sigma_t = V(C_r + beta B_r),
   649	Q_t = a_0 beta^2+b_0 beta+c_0,
   650	prove Sigma_t cap V(Q_t) has no nonzero point.
   651	```
   652	
   653	The unit `a_0=-alpha_t` is uniform for `t>=3`, and `d_Gamma(t)` is known.  The
   654	all-t nonvanishing is not proved.  LENGTH-SPLIT does not close the gap.
   655	
   656	Target B is reduced to an exact radical-membership certificate:
