+# K16 split-tail coefficients and nonvanishing on the Eagon--Northcott curve
+
+Date: 2026-09-04  
+Lane: `k16-brcr-closedform-sol56-20260903`  
+Status: PARTIAL -- closed layer/generating form derived; uniform nonvanishing remains open
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+```text
+DERIVED       An exact two-layer spine and finite path-sum formula for every
+              a_r,b_r,c_r (hence B_r,C_r), uniform in (t,r); equivalently an
+              explicit generating function in r.  It uses only the charged
+              coefficient arrays and the proved scalar pivots.
+
+CORRECTION    Lowering the b3-degree by one raises residual weight by t+1, not
+              by one spine band.  Thus b_r and c_r are NOT one and two further
+              O(r) spine steps after a_r.  Already b_0 needs the complete
+              tangent spine through b2 and c_0 needs the complete constant
+              spine through b2.  The available honest closed form is therefore
+              a t-indexed triangular recurrence/path sum, not a rational
+              function of the two scalar indices (t,r) alone.
+
