   567	
   568	## 4. Restriction to the Eagon--Northcott curve
   569	
   570	### 4.1 Rank-one kernel and the forced parameter \(\beta\)
   571	
   572	At a rank-one point of \(N\), a finite lift has kernel \((1:\beta)\) and
   573	
   574	\[
   575	 C_r+\beta B_r=0\quad(1\leq r<t).                                      \tag{4.1}
   576	\]
   577	
   578	If \(B_s\ne0\), then \(\beta=-C_s/B_s\), and all such ratios agree.  This is
   579	a cover by the opens \(D(B_s)\), not a single global fraction.  On that chart,
   580	
   581	\[
   582	 W_s=B_s^2Q_t,\qquad
   583	 Q_t=a_0\beta^2+b_0\beta+c_0.                                          \tag{4.2}
   584	\]
   585	
   586	If all \(B_r=0\) but some \(C_s\ne0\), the kernel is \((0:1)\), there is no
   587	finite \(b_3\)-lift, and \(W_s=a_0C_s^2\ne0\).  If all \(B_r=C_r=0\) at a
   588	nonzero point, this is rank zero (criterion RANK clause (i)); over an algebraic
   589	closure the unit-leading quadratic has a root and produces a genuine tail
   590	obstruction.  These branches cannot be merged.
   591	
   592	### 4.2 Cleared eliminants \(W_r\)
   593	
   594	The algebraic identity
   595	
   596	\[
   597	 W_r=B_r^2T_{t,2t-1}
   598	 -G_r\{a_0G_r-2a_0C_r+b_0B_r\}                                        \tag{4.3}
   599	\]
   600	
   601	shows (4.2) without division.  After base change to an algebraic closure of
   602	each factor of \(A_t\), put
   603	
   604	\[
   605	 \mathfrak m=(b_4,q_{2,0},\ldots,q_{t-1,0}),\qquad
   606	 K_t=I_2(N)+(W_1,\ldots,W_{t-1}).                                      \tag{4.4}
   607	\]
   608	
   609	The correct collective RANK target (clauses (i) and (ii) together) is
   610	
   611	\[
   612	 \sqrt{K_t}=\mathfrak m,                                                \tag{4.5}
   613	\]
   614	
   615	equivalently \(V(K_t)=\{0\}\), or
   616	
   617	\[
   618	 \operatorname{Proj}(P_t/K_t)=\varnothing,
   619	 \qquad (K_t:\mathfrak m^\infty)=P_t.                                 \tag{4.6}
   620	\]
   621	
   622	All \(W_r\) have positive weight and vanish at the cone vertex, so no one of
   623	them is a literal unit of the affine graded coordinate ring.  A gcd is also
   624	the wrong invariant: the coordinate ring can be reducible/nonfactorial, and
   625	even in a polynomial UFD gcd \(1\) does not say that a multivariable ideal has
   626	no common projective zero.  The object in (4.5) is the ideal generated by all
   627	row-chart eliminants.
   628	
   629	For the Q-nonvanishing clause alone, let
   630	
   631	\[
   632	 J_0=(B_1,\ldots,B_{t-1},C_1,\ldots,C_{t-1}).                            \tag{4.6a}
   633	\]
   634	
   635	The rank-one locus is the determinantal locus minus \(V(J_0)\).  Its exact
   636	projective residual is therefore
   637	
   638	\[
   639	 \operatorname{Proj}\left(P_t/((K_t:J_0^\infty))\right)=\varnothing.     \tag{4.6b}
   640	\]
   641	
   642	If clause (i), \(V(J_0)=\{0\}\), is already known, (4.6b) is equivalent to
   643	(4.5).  Without clause (i), (4.5) would silently assert both open clauses.
   644	
   645	### 4.3 Unit/nonunit test on \(\Gamma\)
   646	
   647	The \(W_1\)-only proposal fails exactly already at \(t=3\).  Let
   648	
   649	\[
   650	 p=(b_4,q_{2,0})=(0,1).
   651	\]
   652	
   653	By weights, \(B_1(p)=C_1(p)=0\), while the exact axis coefficients of
   654	\(B_2,C_2\) are nonzero.  Thus \(p\in\Gamma\), \(\operatorname{rank}N(p)=1\),
   655	and \(W_1(p)=0\), but the valid chart is \(D(B_2)\).  Exact SymPy reduction in
   656	\(A_3=\mathbf Q[d]/(3d^2-4)\) gives
   657	
   658	\[
   659	 Q_3(p,-C_2/B_2)=
   660	 {247708991746515982000-458617889090405137250d
   661	  \over339689253270252579894963},                                      \tag{4.7}
   662	\]
   663	
   664	with norm
   665	
   666	\[
   667	 -{1128865220069406498250000
   668	 \over594567950987267927914970692827}\ne0.                              \tag{4.8}
   669	\]
   670	
   671	Moreover the computation checks exactly
   672	
   673	\[
   674	 W_2(p)-B_2(p)^2Q_3(p,-C_2/B_2)=0,
   675	 \qquad W_2(p)\ne0.                                                     \tag{4.9}
   676	\]
   677	
   678	The full record is
   679	`box/k16brcr-20260903/t3_q2_axis_control.json`.  Hence the zero of \(W_1\) is
   680	not a candidate (V0)-failure after the denominator branch is handled: the
   681	forced lift satisfies the linear rows but not the top row.  This is the direct
   682	cone check requested in item (3).
   683	
   684	### 4.4 Direct cone check of any vanishing locus
   685	
   686	No actual zero of \(Q_t\) on \(\Gamma\) was found.  Charged results prove the
   687	nonvanishing exactly at \(t=3,4\) and by the stated properness promotion at
   688	\(t=5,6\); they do not imply the all-\(t\) assertion.  The layer formula exposes
   689	why it does not collapse to a scalar polynomial in \(t\): the projectivized
   690	determinantal curve has weighted degree
   691	
   692	\[
   693	 d_\Gamma(t)={{3t+1\choose t-1}-{2t\choose t-1}\over t+1},              \tag{4.10}
   694	\]
   695	
   696	and its points have coordinates defined by full-support, full-spine forms.
   697	Nothing in (3.18)--(3.23) parametrizes those points by \(t\) alone.
   698	
   699	A chart-safe homogeneous formulation is useful for future work.  With kernel
   700	coordinate \([u:v]\), impose
   701	
   702	\[
   703	 uC_r+vB_r=0,\qquad
   704	 \widehat Q_t=a_0v^2+b_0uv+c_0u^2.                                    \tag{4.11}
   705	\]
   706	
   707	The chart \(u=0\) is automatically safe because
   708	\(\widehat Q_t=a_0v^2\); on \(u\ne0\), \(v/u=\beta\).  The remaining exact
   709	residual is to prove that (4.11) has no nonzero rank-one base point,
   710	equivalently (4.6b), factorwise.  With rank-zero clause (i) added, this becomes
   711	(4.5).  Neither the leading coefficient norms nor LENGTH-SPLIT proves that
   712	disjointness.
   713	
   714	## 5. The \(t=2\) control
   715	
   716	### 5.1 \(y=1/5\)
   717	
   718	Here \(d=-1\), and the generated tail is
   719	
   720	\[
   721	 T_{2,3}=-{77\over80}b_3b_4^3+{413\over128}b_4^6,
   722	\]
   723	\[
   724	 T_{2,2}={7\over40}b_3b_4^4-{49\over128}b_4^7.                          \tag{5.1}
   725	\]
   726	
   727	Thus
   728	
   729	\[
   730	 a_0=a_1=0,\quad b_0=-{77\over80}b_4^3,\quad
   731	 c_0={413\over128}b_4^6,\quad B_1=C_1=W_1=0.                           \tag{5.2}
   732	\]
   733	
   734	Both rows vanish on \(b_4=0\); the \(b_3\)-axis lies in the tail cone and its
   735	dimension is one.  The unit-leading hypothesis behind TAIL-SPLIT/FITT fails,
   736	so it would be invalid to apply the rank-two criterion on this factor.
   737	
   738	### 5.2 \(y=2/5\)
   739	
   740	Here \(d=1\), and
   741	
   742	\[
   743	 Q_2=-{28\over625}\beta^2
   744	 -{34944\over3048625}b_4^3\beta
   745	 +{675939222\over14870583025}b_4^6,                                   \tag{5.3}
   746	\]
   747	\[
   748	 B_1=-{12047616\over11051265625}b_4^4,qquad
   749	 C_1={232682357376\over53905863465625}b_4^7.                            \tag{5.4}
   750	\]
   751	
   752	For \(b_4\ne0\),
   753	
   754	\[
   755	 \beta=-C_1/B_1={16030255\over4048574}b_4^3,
   756	\]
   757	\[
   758	 Q_2(p,\beta)=-{2877765360673\over4097737858369}b_4^6\ne0,              \tag{5.5}
   759	\]
   760	
   761	and
   762	
   763	\[
   764	 W_1=-{60631935093139183828992
   765	 \over72646052899365103388916015625}b_4^{14}.                           \tag{5.6}
   766	\]
   767	
   768	Thus \(V(W_1)=\{0\}\) in the one-variable base cone, the tail quotient has
   769	length \(14\), and the cone is zero-dimensional.  Notice that the successful
   770	\(W_1\) in (5.6) is still not a unit; it is a positive-degree parameter.
   771	
   772	## 6. Verdict and exact residual
   773	
   774	The requested coefficient derivation succeeds in the strongest form licensed
   775	by the indexed source: the complete two-layer spine (3.14)--(3.15), finite
   776	path sum (3.18), coefficient formulas (3.19)--(3.21), and row generating
   777	function (3.22) determine \(b_r,c_r,B_r,C_r\) exactly for arbitrary \(t,r\).
   778	They also prove why the hoped-for bounded-depth rational formula does not
   779	follow: a loss of one power of \(b_3\) costs \(t+1\) units of residual weight,
   780	so the final high pivot is already visible in \(b_0,c_0\).
   781	
   782	The nonvanishing attack produces a definitive chart correction and an exact
   783	negative control for the proposed proxy: \(W_1\) vanishes at a rank-one
   784	\(t=3\) point where \(Q_3\) does not.  It produces no actual \(Q_t\)-zero for
   785	\(t\geq3\).  Therefore the full chain
   786	
   787	```text
   788	Q_t nonvanishing on Gamma for all t
   789	  => (V0) => (8.1) => constant spine / normalizer / second affine spine => (T)
   790	```
   791	
   792	cannot be promoted in this report.  The exact residual is:
   793	
   794	\[
   795	 \boxed{\text{For every integer }t\geq3\text{ and every factor of }A_t,
   796	 \quad
   797	 \operatorname{Proj}\bigl(P_t/((I_2(N)+(W)):J_0^\infty)\bigr)
   798	 =\varnothing.}                                                        \tag{6.1}
   799	\]
   800	
   801	Equivalently, prove the homogeneous incidence system (4.11) has no nonvertex
   802	rank-one zero.  Together with clause (i), (6.1) is the m-primary equality
   803	(4.5), hence the full tail statement.  This is
   804	OPEN[K16-Q-NONVANISHING-ON-GAMMA].  The verdict is **PARTIAL**, not “resolved”
   805	and not “reduced to one scalar polynomial in \(t\).”
   806	
   807	## Appendix A. Machine-readable formulas and tables
   808	
   809	The explicit files in Section 2 are self-contained once their displayed
   810	quadratic relation for `yy` is imposed.  `support_leaders.json` contains the
   811	same leader table with separate norm fields.  The raw `brcr_t*.out` transcripts
   812	also include every \(W_r\), but the clean explicit files intentionally stop at
   813	the requested \(T,a,b,c,B,C\) data to keep writes bounded.
   814	
   815	The \(t=2\) exact polynomial files are
   816	`explicit_tail_t2_split_b0.txt` (\(y=1/5\)) and
   817	`explicit_tail_t2_split_b1.txt` (\(y=2/5\)).
   818	
   819	## Appendix B. Commands, resource bounds, and output hashes
   820	
   821	No Singular process was backgrounded.  No job exceeded one core, the 1200 s
   822	cap, or 22 seconds actual wall time in the Singular batch.  No large standard
   823	basis was started.  Before sealing, `ps` and the charged `killmine.py` detector
   824	are used to confirm that no lane job remains alive.

