   118	
   119	**(b) The leading coefficients are uniformly computable.**  The eliminated
   120	spine variables have the weights `wt C_j=j`, `wt q_(j,0)=j (t<=j<=2t)`,
   121	`wt b2=2t+1`, `wt b1=3t+1`, `wt T(0)=t`, and each solved value is a weighted
   122	form of its own weight in the residual variables (banked grading (2.1)).  A
   123	monomial of `[b3^2]T_(t,2t-1-r)` has `(b4,q)`-weight `r`.  A solved value can
   124	contribute to it only through its own monomials of `b3`-degree `<=2` and
   125	`(b4,q)`-weight `<=r`: for `C_j` (pure, weight `j<t+1`) that needs `j<=r`; for
   126	`q_(j,0)`, `t<=j<=2t`, the pure part has weight `j>=t>r`, and only its
   127	`b3`-linear part `b3*(weight j-t-1)` can enter, needing `j<=t+1+r`; `b2`'s
   128	`b3`-part has weight `t>r`; `T(0)` is pure of weight `t>r`; `b1`'s `b3^2`-part
   129	has weight `t-1`, entering only at `r=t-1`.  The same count applied to the band
   130	equations `rho_j+p_j z_j=0` shows that the `(b4,q)`-weight-`<=r` parts of
   131	`C_1..C_r` and the `b3`-linear parts of `q_(t+1,0)..q_(t+1+r,0)` are determined
   132	by each other alone.  Therefore, for `0<=r<=t-2`,
   133	
   134	```text
   135	a_r = [b3^2] T_(t,2t-1-r) is computed by the truncated spine of 2r+1 scalars
   136	      {C_1..C_r ; b3-parts of q_(t+1,0)..q_(t+1+r,0)},  all other spine
   137	      variables set to 0, and only the b4-degree-<=r window of the arrays
   138	      (binomials binom(q,m) with q-m<=r) enters.                        (3.2)
   139	```
   140	
   141	Every entry of that finite triangular solve is a polynomial in `t` of degree
   142	`<=r` over `A_t` divided by the banked unit pivots, so **for each fixed `r`,
   143	`a_r` is a single rational function of `(t,d)`**, valid for all `t>=r+2`.
   144	`r=0` is the b3-axis chart and gives `a_0=-alpha_t` (driver sign):
   145	
   146	```text
   147	alpha_t = t(3t+1)[(27t^3-30t^2+t-2)d+(6t^3+13t^2-3t+2)] / (12q^2(3t-1)^2(3t+2)),
   148	a unit of A_t for every t>=3 (banked norm (4.8)).                        (3.3)
   149	```
   150	
   151	checked here symbolically at `t=3,4,5,6,7`: the driver's `[b3^2]T_(t,2t-1)`
   152	plus `alpha_t` reduces to `0` in `A_t`.  `r=1` gives `a_1 = mu_t b4`, one
   153	scalar; `r=2` gives `a_2 = mu'_t b4^2 + mu''_t q_(2,0)`.  Their closed forms
   154	were **not** derived (that needs a symbolic-`t` engine for (3.2); typed OPEN),
   155	but the exact values are:
   156	
   157	| `t` | `Res_y(H_t, mu_t)` (`r=1`, coefficient of `b3^2 b4`) | `Res_y(H_t, mu'_t)` (`b3^2 b4^2`) | `Res_y(H_t, mu''_t)` (`b3^2 q_(2,0)`) |
   158	|---:|---|---|---|
   159	| 3 | `159028943/148574272` | `-4250137195970063/4803319854964400` | `-11399375/34603212` |
   160	| 4 | `-804680656/847247445` | `27103436928548351176/4441316531861763675` | `-1273869353120/1299812628609` |
   161	| 5 | `-109301941200/20300415751` | `56469816361018858800/29246083658911332521` | `-10644469200/3246539263` |
   162	| 6 | `-700061590663/53458672345` | `-85303805865939146725660/13070843663072030433637` | `-327293088530100/46095984051013` |
   163	| 7 | `-46766375117231/1875690010800` | `-9998773302319921660374647429/483748757167964713795968750` | `-1596919376374322/124493551171875` |
   164	
   165	All nonzero: `a_0,a_1,a_2` are units times monomials at `t=3..7`.  At `t=2`,
   166	`y=2/5`: `a_0=-28/625`, `a_1=-252/3625 b4`; at `y=1/5`: `a_0=a_1=0` and the
   167	top rows are LINEAR in `b3` (`alpha_2` vanishes there, as banked).
   168	
   169	**(c) What (a)-(b) give and do not give.**  Since `a_0=alpha_t` is a unit,
   170	`b3` is integral over `A_t[q]/(Q_0)`, the projection `V(J)->A^(t-2)_q`
   171	(`J=I_(t,+)|_(b4=1)`) is finite, and `J=(1)` iff `J cap A_t[q]=(1)`.  The
   172	`b_r,c_r` carry the whole spine (all `2t+1` solves), exactly as the
   173	`b4`-axis report found for the pure `b4` coefficients; no closed form in `t`
   174	exists for them by this route, and none is claimed.
   175	
   176	## 4. Verification against the charged records (t=2..7)
   177	
   178	`singular_terminal_driver.py --compare-record` (the charged comparison, rows
   179	subtracted band by band in the declared ring) printed `BANKED_ROWS_MATCH`
   180	against `terminal_laurent_t4.json`, `terminal_laurent_t5.json` and, on both
   110	
   111	To verify (2.4), use `R_0=LC` in the charged Euler identity.  Its three
   112	bilinear terms combine as
   113	
   114	```text
   115	R_0 B-LR_0 B'+2LR_0'B=3LCB+2L^2C'B-L^2CB',
   116	```
   117	
   118	whose `L^m` coefficient is the convolution in (2.4); moreover
   119	`C+(5/2)(LC)'` contributes `(5m+7)C_m/2`.  This is a coefficient proof for
   120	every `m`, not a CAS pattern.
   121	
   122	Define
   123	
   124	```text
   125	V=L^2C-yb3,       Y=LS-b3B-gb2,       Z=LB-gb3,
   126	N=-VY'+V'Y+2U'Z,
   127	P0'=(N-N(0))/(2yL),
   128	R=VP0'-U'Y-yg=-E_t.                                  (2.5)
   129	```
   130	
   131	The displayed numerator `N-N(0)` is divisible by `L`.  The separate charged
   132	`D1` evaluation, already incorporated in (2.5), gives
   133	
   134	```text
   135	b1=-b3(U_1+b3 C_0)/y.                                 (2.6)
   136	```
   137	
   138	For completeness, changing the omitted constant `B_0` by `delta` changes the
   139	Euler right side by `delta(3LC+2L^2C')`; hence
   140	`delta S=(delta/y)LC`, `delta Y=(delta/y)V`, and `delta Z=delta L`.
   141	Consequently `delta N=2 delta L U'`, `delta P0'=delta U'/y`, and the two
   142	variations in `E_t=-VP0'+U'Y+yg` cancel.  Thus the terminal family is genuinely
   143	independent of `B_0`.  The charged gauge diagonal `q/y` is still a unit, but
   144	need not be computed to obtain the terminal rows.
   145	
   146	Here is the completely coefficientwise version of (2.5):
   147	
   148	```text
   149	V_m=C_(m-2)-yb3 delta_(m,0),
   150	Y_m=S_(m-1)-b3 B_m-gb2 delta_(m,0),
   151	Z_m=B_(m-1)-gb3 delta_(m,0),
   152	
   153	N_m=-sum_(a+b=m)V_a(b+1)Y_(b+1)
   154	    +sum_(a+b=m)(a+1)V_(a+1)Y_b
   155	    +2sum_(a+b=m)(a+1)U_(a+1)Z_b,
   156	(P0')_r=N_(r+1)/(2y),
   157	R_m=sum_(a+b=m)V_a(P0')_b
   158	    -sum_(a+b=m)(a+1)U_(a+1)Y_b-yg delta_(m,0).      (2.7)
   159	```
   160	
   161	All convolution indices in (2.4),(2.7) are nonnegative, and every array is
   162	zero outside its displayed polynomial range.
   163	
   164	### 2.1 The high-weight recursion
   165	
   166	Order the variables
   167	
   168	```text
   169	z_j=c_j                    (1<=j<t),
   170	z_j=u_j                    (t<=j<=2t),

